  "summary": "A former Oak Park village trustee writes an opinion letter criticizing the Village Board's 5-2 vote on August 5 to cancel Oak Park's contract with Flock Safety ALPR cameras. The author argues the decision ignores expert recommendations, hurts an understaffed police department, and undermines regional crime-prevention collaboration.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "On Aug. 5, the Oak Park Village Board voted 5-2 to cancel our contract with Flock Safety, the automated license plate reader (ALPR) technology recommended by both our Police Department and the independent 2022 community safety study conducted by BerryDunn.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Neighboring communities have implemented Flock cameras. Canceling this contract doesn't protect our privacy; it just makes joint crime prevention efforts harder for Oak Park.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
  ],
